  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>X</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;pressure, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math>&nbsp;is volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is universal gas constant and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> is temperature. The physical quantity equivalent&nbsp;to the ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is:</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "x8Dk4",
      "text": "Pressure gradient",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "RlS9V",
      "text": "Energy",
